Subject: URGENT: Black Particulate Matter Observed in Sterile Ceftriaxone Injection Vials (Batch #CFT-9082)
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 14:15:20 +0000

Dear Quality Assurance & Medical Safety Team,

I am writing to report a Critical Quality Defect regarding Ceftriaxone Sodium for Injection 1g (Batch Lot Number: CFT-9082, Expiry Date: 11/2027, Manufactured: 05/2026).

During routine reconstitution in the Intensive Care Unit at St. Jude Regional Hospital on July 26, 2026, clinical pharmacy staff noticed distinct black, thread-like particulate matter floating inside two un-administered 1g vials after dilution with Sterile Water for Injection. The seals on both vials were visually intact prior to preparation.

Product Details:
- Customer Name: St. Jude Regional Hospital (Account #HOSP-9921)
- Complaint Source: Hospital Pharmacy Unit
- Product Name: Ceftriaxone Sodium for Injection
- Strength/Grade: 1g / Sterile Injectable Grade
- Batch/Lot Number: CFT-9082
- Quantity Affected: 2 vials out of 100-vial carton (Carton Serial #C-44019)
- Complaint Date: 2026-07-27

Impact & Action Taken:
The affected lot was immediately quarantined across our pharmacy stock. No patient was administered the contaminated solution; however, due to the high risk of pulmonary emboli or systemic inflammatory response associated with intravenous particulate matter, this represents a severe patient safety hazard.

Please send return authorization and immediate instructions for sample evaluation and batch investigation.

